{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/335561-christmas-on-the-world-of-darkness","id":335561,"title":"Christmas on the World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-09T16:21:42-08:00","id":335561,"title":"Christmas on the World of Darkness","content":"So..how have you handled christmas on the WoD? , have you ever done it?<br /> <br /> I got a vampire player who is gonna get visited by a Wraith, a Changeling and a Demon on a night.<br /> I got some players discussing on how the technocratic union would react to a beeing flying at the speed of sound dropping gifts<br /> and i got Santa and The Garous vs the Black Spiral Dancers on the north pole....<br /> <br /> <br /> ...so, any thoughts on yer christmas games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T17:58:21-08:00","id":335611,"title":"","content":"I've run light-hearted seasonal sessions for other games, but for <b>The World Of Darkness</b> I tend to focus on the religious iconography, the winter weather and the crass commercialism. I'm planning a bleak Christmas special for my current <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> game for next session. <a href=\"http://thewatchhouserpg.blogspot.co.uk/2011/12/vampire-in-bleak-midwinter.html\" target=\"_blank\">I wrote a post about the season for vampires on my blog</a> with the aim of making it an ironic backdrop for a story, or an inspiration for one. There is hope... just maybe not for the Kindred,<br /> <br /> There's a great <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?711389-World-of-Darkness-Is-there-a-Santa-Claus\" target=\"_blank\">RPGnet thread</a> from last year about what Santa could be in various WOD games, varying from the wildly supernatural and twisted to some pretty low-key ideas.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://thewatchhouserpg.blogspot.co.uk/2014/12/vampire-red-nativity.html\" target=\"_blank\">Finally bigged up my previous Vampire Christmas Special ideas</a>. Current <b>V20</b> players stay out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","user":"Craig Oxbrow","date":".  About 700 words of new stuff 12-22-2014, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T04:49:33-08:00","id":335974,"title":"","content":"I'm not really a Christmas person, but I think I might have a Yule festival for my werewolf players so that they can see how it works at the Sept of the Green. Plus, the pack alpha is attempting to convince Helios to work with them, so what better time to celebrate than on the morning the sun begins to return to full strength in their part of the world? I want to have a big New Year party crashed by some vamps, too, just to see what they do and how they behave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T09:50:57-08:00","id":336120,"title":"","content":"I like Christmas, but my W:tA game is set in 1840. The modern holiday was in its infancy, only starting to be recognized and celebrated in some southern states. I will likely have my Garou perform the customary winter solstice rites, but that is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T10:08:29-08:00","id":336134,"title":"","content":"St Nick is a Changeling, maybe, he is Santa while Seelie and Krumpas when Unseelie.<br /> <br /> He's using Magiteck from a Celestial Chorister which has massive amounts of Correspondence and Time magic applied to the sled and the reindeer. It generates such massive amounts of Paradox that it can only be used once a year, at night. The Technocracy won't touch him because the impending psychic backlash from &quot;No Santa&quot; would collapse the entire Horizon in on itself. They're not sure why this is, but the one time they tried taking shots at him allowed the Roswell aliens to come in and crash land THRU THE GAUNTLET, so they're not taking the risk again.<br /> <br /> The vampires can't touch him because Rudolph's nose is generating the equivalent of a noontime sun in the desert and burns them to ash instantly.....even the Methuselahs. Plus, Caine is, for some odd reason, permanently on the &quot;nice list&quot;, so he doesn't want anyone to bother Santa.<br /> <br /> The Garou won't molest him, either, because of all the silver bells all over the sleigh and harnesses, plus the few who've gotten close enough to smell him are convinced the fur lining his outfit is Silver Fang skin.<br /> <br /> Obviously, as a bastion of magic, dreams and imagination, the other Changelings adore him and will always assist whenever possible. More than a few Boggans have disappeared on X-mas night, it's assumed they signed up to be a toy-maker elf.<br /> <br /> The one hunter who actually had the gaul to try to go after him came back stripped of all his powers with lashes all over his body.<br /> <br /> The mummies have never encountered him and no one seems to be interesting in changing that.<br /> <br /> Lucifer knows his whole story and has the utmost respect and <i>fear </i>of him. Yes, the Fallen who does not fear God is afraid of Santa Claus. All the Fallen who know this hide on X-mas Eve. All who don't and try to mess with Santa learn the reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T10:50:10-08:00","id":336146,"title":"","content":"I can appreciate your take on Santa, PapaBear, but everyone knows Santa is a marauder!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:27:22-08:00","id":336297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/335561-christmas-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=336146#post336146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can appreciate your take on Santa, PapaBear, but everyone knows Santa is a marauder!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I did say &quot;maybe&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T02:11:15-08:00","id":336849,"title":"","content":"Pentex donates a lot of food, clothing and toys to the under-privileged at Christmas, which they write off as a tax deduction later.<br /> <br /> According to the local Kindred it makes the 'herd' taste funny.<br /> <br /> Drew your own conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 12-12-2014, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T06:52:52-08:00","id":336983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/335561-christmas-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=336849#post336849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex donates a lot of food, clothing and toys to the under-pillaged at Christmas, which they write off as a tax deduction later.<br /> <br /> According to the local Kindred it makes the 'herd' taste funny.<br /> <br /> Drew your own conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's a typo, but I adore the idea of the masses being called the &quot;under <i>pillaged</i>&quot; by Pentex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>